order.status = refunded\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs24 \cf0 Access should then be revoked or suspended according to the application's refund policy.\
For this project, the safest default is:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f4\fs26 \cf0 \
refunded\
    
\f5 \uc0\u8595 
\f4 \
revoke paid access\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs24 \cf0 rather than allowing a refunded account to retain paid privileges.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs48 \cf0 25. The Firestore Transaction\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs24 \cf0 Successful payment processing must use a 
\f0\b Firestore transaction
\f2\b0 .\
When a valid 
\f4\fs26 finished
\f2\fs24  payment is received:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f4\fs26 \cf0 \
BEGIN TRANSACTION\
       
\f5 \uc0\u9474 
\f4 \
       
\f5 \uc0\u9500 \u9472 \u9472 
\f4  Read payment\
       
\f5 \uc0\u9500 \u9472 \u9472 
\f4  Read order\
       
\f5 \uc0\u9500 \u9472 \u9472 
\f4  Read user\
       
\f5 \uc0\u9474 
\f4 \
       
\f5 \uc0\u9500 \u9472 \u9472 
\f4  Check whether already fulfilled\
       
\f5 \uc0\u9474 
\f4 \
       
\f5 \uc0\u9500 \u9472 \u9472 
\f4  Update payment\
       
\f5 \uc0\u9500 \u9472 \u9472 
\f4  Update order\
       
\f5 \uc0\u9500 \u9472 \u9472 
\f4  Update user\
       
\f5 \uc0\u9492 \u9472 \u9472 
\f4  Create entitlement\
       
\f5 \uc0\u9474 
\f4 \
COMMIT\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs24 \cf0 The important reason is atomicity.\
We don't want this:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f4\fs26 \cf0 \
payment = completed\
order = paid\
user = active\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs24 \cf0 to partially execute.\
For example, we don't want:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f4\fs26 \cf0 \
payment = completed\
order = paid\
user = pending_payment\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs24 \cf0 because the function crashed between operations.\
The transaction keeps the business state consistent.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs48 \cf0 26. Exact Activation Rule\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs24 \cf0 This is the most important rule in the entire payment system:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 An account may only transition from 
\f6\fs26 pending_payment
\f0\fs24  to 
\f6\fs26 active
\f0\fs24  after a valid NOWPayments payment has reached 
\f6\fs26 finished
\f0\fs24 , the IPN signature has been verified, the payment has been independently validated, and the corresponding Firestore transaction has successfully committed.
\f2\b0 \
In shorthand:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f4\fs26 \cf0 \
finished\
   +\
valid IPN\
   +\
valid payment\
   +\
valid order\
   +\
sufficient payment\
   +\
valid asset\
   +\
Firestore transaction\
   =\
ACCOUNT ACTIVE\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs24 \cf0 Nothing else can activate the account.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs48 \cf0 27. Idempotency\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs24 \cf0 The webhook must be 
\f0\b idempotent
\f2\b0 .\
This means processing the same payment event multiple times must not produce multiple account activations or duplicate fulfillment.\
Example:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f4\fs26 \cf0 \
IPN #1\
finished\
    
\f5 \uc0\u8595 
\f4 \
activate account\
\
IPN #2\
finished\
    
\f5 \uc0\u8595 
\f4 \
account already active\
    
\f5 \uc0\u8595 
\f4 \
DO NOTHING\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs24 \cf0 NOWPayments documents recurrent notifications when errors occur while processing notifications, so our backend must expect repeated callbacks.\
The transaction should therefore check something such as:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f4\fs26 \cf0 \
order.status === "paid"\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs24 \cf0 before performing fulfillment again.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs48 \cf0 28. Payment Audit Trail\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs24 \cf0 The application should maintain a dedicated:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f4\fs26 \cf0 \
paymentEvents/\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs24 \cf0 collection.\
This is separate from the current 
\f4\fs26 payments/\{paymentId\}
\f2\fs24  document.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 Why?\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs24 \cf0 The payment document represents:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 The current truth about the payment.
\f2\b0 \
The audit trail represents:\

\f0\b The history of everything that happened to the payment.
\f2\b0 \
These are fundamentally different purposes.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs48 \cf0 29. Example Payment History\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs24 \cf0 Suppose a payment goes through:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f4\fs26 \cf0 \
waiting\
   
\f5 \uc0\u8595 
\f4 \
confirming\
   
\f5 \uc0\u8595 
\f4 \
confirmed\
   
\f5 \uc0\u8595 
\f4 \
sending\
   
\f5 \uc0\u8595 
\f4 \
finished\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs24 \cf0 The payment document eventually says:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f4\fs26 \cf0 \
\{\
  providerStatus: "finished",\
  internalStatus: "completed"\
\}\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs24 \cf0 But without an audit trail, we don't know how it got there.\
With the audit trail:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f4\fs26 \cf0 \
paymentEvents/\
\
event_001\
  status: waiting\
  receivedAt: ...\
\
event_002\
  status: confirming\
  receivedAt: ...\
\
event_003\
  status: confirmed\
  receivedAt: ...\
\
event_004\
  status: sending\
  receivedAt: ...\
\
event_005\
  status: finished\
  receivedAt: ...\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs24 \cf0 We now have a complete payment history.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs48 \cf0 30. Why the Audit Trail Matters\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf0 1. Debugging\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs24 \cf0 If a customer says:\
"I paid but my account wasn't activated."\
we can investigate exactly what happened.\
We can see:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f4\fs26 \cf0 \
IPN received\

\f5 \uc0\u8595 
\f4 \
signature valid\

\f5 \uc0\u8595 
\f4 \
payment confirmed\

\f5 \uc0\u8595 
\f4 \
finished received\

\f5 \uc0\u8595 
\f4 \
transaction attempted\

\f5 \uc0\u8595 
\f4 \
transaction failed\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs24 \cf0 Instead of guessing.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 2. Payment disputes\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs24 \cf0 Suppose a customer claims:\
"I paid the full amount."\
We can inspect:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f4\fs26 \cf0 \
expected amount\
actually paid\
pay currency\
provider status\
payment ID\
order ID\
timestamps\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs24 \cf0 and determine what actually happened.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 3. Duplicate webhook investigation\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs24 \cf0 If NOWPayments sends the same notification several times, the audit trail lets us see:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f4\fs26 \cf0 \
finished\
finished\
finished\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs24 \cf0 while the order was fulfilled only once.\
This proves that idempotency worked.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 4. Security investigation\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs24 \cf0 If someone attempts to send a fake webhook, we can record:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f4\fs26 \cf0 \
signatureValid: false\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs24 \cf0 and reject it.\
This gives us an internal security record.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 5. Operational visibility\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs24 \cf0 The audit trail lets us answer questions like:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f4\fs26 \cf0 \
How many payments entered confirming today?\
How many became finished?\
How many failed?\
How many were underpaid?\
How many expired?\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs24 \cf0 without relying exclusively on NOWPayments' dashboard.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 6. Recovery\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs24 \cf0 Imagine a Cloud Function fails after NOWPayments reports:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f4\fs26 \cf0 \
finished\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs24 \cf0 The notification may be retried.\
Even if we need to manually investigate the incident, our audit history tells us exactly where processing stopped.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 7. Financial reconciliation\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs24 \cf0 The audit trail gives us a historical record that can later be compared against:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f4\fs26 \cf0 \
NOWPayments payment history\
+\
our orders\
+\
our payment records\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs24 \cf0 This becomes extremely valuable as transaction volume grows.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs48 \cf0 31. Audit Event Structure\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs24 \cf0 Use:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f4\fs26 \cf0 \
paymentEvents/\{eventId\}\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs24 \cf0 Example:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f4\fs26 \cf0 \
\{\
  paymentId: "payment123",\
  orderId: "order123",\
  userId: "uid123",\
\
  provider: "nowpayments",\
\
  providerStatus: "finished",\
\
  previousProviderStatus: "sending",\
\
  internalStatus: "completed",\
\
  eventType: "payment_status_changed",\
\
  signatureValid: true,\
\
  receivedAt: Timestamp,\
\
  processedAt: Timestamp,\
\
  processingResult: "success",\
\
  payload: \{\
    // sanitized NOWPayments payload\
  \}\
\}\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs24 \cf0 Do not store secrets in the audit record.\
In particular, never store:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f4\fs26 \cf0 \
NOWPayments API key\
IPN secret\
Firebase Admin credentials\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs24 \cf3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs48 \cf0 32. Audit Trail vs Payment Document\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs24 \cf0 The distinction should remain explicit.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 Payment document\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f4\b0\fs26 \cf0 \
payments/\{paymentId\}\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs24 \cf0 answers:\
"What is the payment's current state?"\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 Audit event\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f4\b0\fs26 \cf0 \
paymentEvents/\{eventId\}\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs24 \cf0 answers:\
"What happened to this payment over time?"\
Therefore:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f4\fs26 \cf0 \
payments/payment123\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs24 \cf0 might currently contain:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f4\fs26 \cf0 \
\{\
  providerStatus: "finished",\
  internalStatus: "completed"\
\}\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs24 \cf0 while:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f4\fs26 \cf0 \
paymentEvents/\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs24 \cf0 contains the historical state transitions.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

