\f0\b\fs48 \cf0 36. Network/Browser Failure\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs24 \cf0 The customer's browser must 
\f0\b not
\f2\b0  control payment completion.\
For example:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f4\fs26 \cf0 \
Customer pays\
     
\f5 \uc0\u8595 
\f4 \
Internet disconnects\
     
\f5 \uc0\u8595 
\f4 \
Browser disappears\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs24 \cf0 The payment processing does not depend on React remaining open.\
NOWPayments continues processing the transaction and can send the IPN to our backend.\
When the user returns:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f4\fs26 \cf0 \
React\
  
\f5 \uc0\u8595 
\f4 \
Firebase Auth\
  
\f5 \uc0\u8595 
\f4 \
Firestore\
  
\f5 \uc0\u8595 
\f4 \
accountStatus\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs24 \cf0 The UI reflects the actual backend state.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs48 \cf0 37. Security Rules\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs24 \cf0 The frontend must never be allowed to directly manipulate:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f4\fs26 \cf0 \
accountStatus\
order.status\
payment.status\
entitlement.status\
paymentEvents\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs24 \cf0 For example, a malicious user must not be able to do:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f4\fs26 \cf0 \
updateDoc(userRef, \{\
  accountStatus: "active"\
\});\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs24 \cf0 and activate themselves.\
These state transitions must happen 
\f0\b server-side through trusted Firebase Cloud Functions
\f2\b0 .\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs48 \cf0 38. Secrets\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs24 \cf0 The following values must remain server-side:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f4\fs26 \cf0 \
NOWPayments API Key\
NOWPayments IPN Secret\
Firebase Admin credentials/configuration\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs24 \cf0 They should be managed through the Firebase/server-side secret configuration rather than committed to the React application.\
Never put the IPN secret in:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f4\fs26 \cf0 \
.env\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs24 \cf0 if that 
\f4\fs26 .env
\f2\fs24  is bundled into the Vite frontend.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs48 \cf0 39. Final Architectural Rules\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs24 \cf0 The AI coding assistant must follow these rules throughout implementation:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 Rule 1\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 Never trust the frontend to confirm payment.
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 Rule 2\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 Never activate an account because the customer reached 
\f6\fs26 success_url
\f0\fs24 .
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 Rule 3\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 Never activate an account on 
\f6\fs26 confirming
\f0\fs24 , 
\f6\fs26 confirmed
\f0\fs24 , or 
\f6\fs26 sending
\f0\fs24 .
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 Rule 4\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 Never automatically fulfill a 
\f6\fs26 partially_paid
\f0\fs24  payment.
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 Rule 5\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 Always verify the NOWPayments IPN signature.
\f2\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 Rule 6\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 Use the NOWPayments payment-status endpoint as an additional verification layer.
